;; A parenthesised suffix with the wrong arity is still an error: one type is
;; not a (key value) pair.  Caught in the reader rather than reaching the
;; elaborator as a mis-arity `(Map int)` application, whose error would point
;; at a form the user never wrote.
(defn main [] : int
  (let [m #map{}:(int)]
    0))
